            "review_title": "Review at Trốn Để Dừng Chân",
            "review_text": "Hoang Quan\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam62 contributions\n0\nA Hidden Oasis in the Heart of Saigon\nDec 2024 • Family\nNestled in a quiet alley of District 10, TRỐN Để Dừng Chân (meaning “a place to escape and pause”) is a gem that perfectly blends rustic charm with vibrant greenery. From the moment you step into this cozy café, you’re greeted by the soothing ambiance of plants, natural light, and vintage décor.\n\nThe menu offers a thoughtful selection of beverages, from fragrant Vietnamese coffee to refreshing kombucha, paired perfectly with a variety of homemade pastries. My personal favorite was the Matcha Latte, which was smooth, earthy, and balanced just right with a touch of sweetness.\n\nWhat makes TRỐN truly unique is its welcoming atmosphere. It’s not just a café; it’s a space where you can work, catch up with friends, or simply retreat from the bustling streets of Saigon. Whether you’re sitting in the lush courtyard or the charming indoor space, every corner is picture-perfect—ideal for a quiet escape or Instagram-worthy photos.\n\nFor those visiting during the mornings, they even have special combos that are both delicious and budget-friendly. The staff here are attentive and friendly, making sure every visit feels personal and memorable.\n\nIf you’re looking for a serene spot to relax, recharge, or connect with the local community, TRỐN Để Dừng Chân is a must-visit in Saigon. I’ll definitely be back!\n\nPro Tips:\n • Visit during the morning to enjoy their special breakfast deals.\n • Don’t forget to snap a picture at the café’s signature “Check-in Mirror” for a fun, unique memory.\n • The café is located in an alley, so keep an eye out for the small sign leading the way!\n\nWould I recommend? Absolutely. A little escape like this is just what you need in a vibrant city like Saigon.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nThey have espresso, americano, latte and capouchino so its easy to get a drink. Vietnamese coffee is also a good choice\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 14, 2025",
